# ai.env — Configuration for ai.sh
# Uncomment and edit to override defaults.

# AI_DIR — Base directory (default: auto-detected from ai.sh location)
# AI_DIR="/Users/p/Development/tools/ai"

# AI_LOG_DIR — Server log directory (default: $AI_DIR/logs)
# AI_LOG_DIR="${AI_DIR}/logs"

# AI_STATE_DIR — State and PID files (default: ~/.local/state)
# AI_STATE_DIR="${HOME}/.local/state"

# AI_PORT — oMLX server port (default: 10081)
# AI_PORT=10081

# ── oMLX server (local mode) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Each of these applies to EVERY profile — they are resolved once, after the
# profile is chosen, so setting one here overrides the profile's own default.
#
# OMLX_BIN — oMLX binary (default: the profile's venv, else `omlx` on PATH)
# OMLX_BIN="${HOME}/.omlx/venv/bin/omlx"
# OMLX_MODEL_DIR — dir oMLX discovers models from (default: ~/.omlx/models)
# OMLX_MODEL_DIR="${HOME}/.omlx/models"
# OMLX_CACHE_DIR — paged SSD KV-cache dir (default: ~/.omlx/cache)
# OMLX_CACHE_DIR="${HOME}/.omlx/cache"
# OMLX_HOT_CACHE — in-RAM hot KV tier size (default: 8GB; model + tier must
#   fit under the memory guard's soft threshold or oMLX evicts models mid-request)
# OMLX_HOT_CACHE="8GB"
# OMLX_SSD_CACHE_MAX — paged SSD cache disk cap (default: 40GB; unset, oMLX
#   claims nearly all free disk)
# OMLX_SSD_CACHE_MAX="40GB"
# OMLX_CACHE_PRUNE_GB — prune the on-disk KV cache to this many GB at each server
#   (re)start, oldest-first (default: numeric part of OMLX_SSD_CACHE_MAX, so it can
#   never disagree with what the server is told). oMLX's own LRU only tracks its
#   live index, so orphaned blocks from prior runs / model-quant switches leak far
#   over the cap; this enforces it. Set 0 to disable.
# OMLX_CACHE_PRUNE_GB=40
# OMLX_MEMORY_GUARD_GB — memory ceiling in GB (default: 48; raise on 128 GB)
# OMLX_MEMORY_GUARD_GB=48
# OMLX_MAX_CONCURRENT — max concurrent requests / continuous batching (default: 2 —
#   one coding turn + the opencode-mem summarizer; don't set to 1 or memory
#   captures serialize with coding turns)
# OMLX_MAX_CONCURRENT=2

# ── Hybrid cloud advisor (used by `ai -hybrid`) ──────────────────────
# `ai -hybrid` adds a manual, prompt-only @advisor subagent on real cloud Claude.
# It needs a ONE-TIME login (no API key, no env var) — uses your Claude plan:
#   opencode auth login   →  Anthropic  (OAuth)
# Every advisor call is logged to $AI_LOG_DIR/advisor-egress.jsonl (append-only
# audit trail). ai.sh sets the path automatically from AI_LOG_DIR; nothing to set
# here. The advisor agent + egress-log plugin are symlinked in only under -hybrid
# and removed on every other launch, so a plain `ai` has no path to the cloud.

# ── opencode-mem privacy: never store/recall memory from these trees ──
# Colon-separated dir prefixes. List your sensitive client-repo roots here so NO
# session in them touches the memory store.
# OPENCODE_MEM_EXCLUDE_DIRS="/Users/p/Development/client-acme:/Users/p/work/secret"

# ── smart-coding RAG: extra directories to keep out of the index ──
# Colon-separated globs, appended to what ProjectDetector emits (see
# scripts/patch-smart-coding-excludes.mjs). Python virtualenv and tool-cache trees
# are already excluded by that patch's built-in set, so this is only for repo-
# specific noise.
#
# Each entry MUST be exactly "**/<dirname>/**" with no wildcard inside <dirname>:
# the indexer reduces every pattern to a bare directory name and exact-matches it
# per directory, so file-level globs like "**/*.min.js" silently do nothing.
#
# Worth considering: i18n locale dumps. Flat translation JSON carries no code
# semantics but chunks heavily — four locale files in one repo produced ~1,290
# chunks, re-embedded on every translation edit (watchFiles is on).
# SMART_CODING_EXCLUDE_PATTERNS="**/locales/**:**/fixtures/**:**/__snapshots__/**"

# Set to "false" to drop the built-in virtualenv/tool-cache excludes entirely.
# SMART_CODING_EXCLUDE_DEFAULTS="false"
